WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.210
The US High Plains.

2
00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:07.090
From 1949 to 2012,
irrigated land multiplied,

3
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.470
watered from an aquifer below.

4
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.410
In Australia, bores tap
the Great Artesian Basin.

5
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.030
Water can flow up without pumping.

6
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:21.470
Since about 1750, we have burned
carbon stored over millions of years.

7
00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:26.690
Through the ice-age cycles, CO₂ stayed
at or below 300 parts per million.

8
00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:32.450
In 2025: 425.7 parts per million.

9
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.290
So what happens when we take from a
store faster than the cycle refills it?

10
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:41.070
In this mission, you'll see
how a store stays in balance.

11
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:47.170
Then you'll trace how cities, farms, pumps
and power stations disturb both cycles.

12
00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:52.190
Your mission: explain what happens when
we take faster than a cycle refills.
